  "note": "Total Eclipse (MOVES.md; the flash on 0-39, invulnerable 0-43). Frames 0-8: Shadow gathers low, claws drawn in to the chest; 9-18: it rises to full height and throws its claws wide, the right up and forward, the left up and back, the shoulder cape plates fanned out and up, the head back (the eye flare and the dark stage are the effects'); it holds there, shuddering, to 36, and drops into a low lunge with the right claw cocked high (37-40). 40-43: it darts 8 m forward (root motion 2 m a frame), the legs trailing. Then four slashes, each its own hit (the box `hit` index), alternating claws from a wide low stance, the body leaning back so the long arms strike close: hit 0 (44-46) the right claw from high to low, hit 1 (49-51) the left from low to high, hit 2 (54-56) and hit 3 (59-61) the same again (each the claw's own box; x 0.4-6.3, y 2.3-10.7 over the four, MOVES.md x 0-6, y 3-10). 62-64: it drops into a crouch with both claws hanging hooked to the floor; hit 4, the finisher (65-69): both claws hauled up from the floor to over its head as it rises (both boxes `hit` 4: x 0.4-5.8, y 0-11.8; MOVES.md x 0-6.5, y 0-12). Recovery 70-105: the arms spread and come down, the plates settle, the rear foot steps in (86-94) and it returns to the guard. No phases: the five hits leave gaps that a single active range cannot describe (verify warns); the active frames are exactly MOVES.md's. The claws touch at the top of the finisher, talons together (allowed).",
